Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The meaning of the "dangerous" flag was written twice - in the schema
field description and in the structured system-prompt rule - and the two
copies disagreed:

  schema:  changes system state ... writes to devices ...
  system:  changes system state or configuration ... writes to raw devices

"writes to devices" literally covers every `2>/dev/null`, and Sonnet 5
follows instructions literally, so the model had to reconcile two
wordings on every call. The reconciled definition (the system prompt's
more precise wording, matching the README's 'raw-device writes') now
lives only in the field description, which is the contract of the
boolean. The system prompt keeps the instruction to assess, and
dangerReason's description absorbs the 'short, whenever dangerous' rule.

Live before/after probe (claude-sonnet-5, 12 runs each): benign
/dev/null redirections flagged 0/9 -> 0/9; raw-disk dd control flagged
3/3 -> 3/3. No regression; the gain is one unambiguous definition.

- test: pin that the definition lives in the schema, not the prompt
---
 src/prompts.ts       | 14 +++++---------
 test/prompts.test.ts |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/prompts.ts b/src/prompts.ts
index 80dbfb3..0f663ff 100644
--- a/src/prompts.ts
+++ b/src/prompts.ts
@@ -38,13 +38,13 @@ export const COMMANDS_SCHEMA: Record<string, unknown> = {
             type: 'boolean',
             description:
               'True when the command deletes or overwrites data, changes ' +
-              'system state, elevates privileges, writes to devices, kills ' +
-              'processes, rewrites published history, or pipes remote ' +
-              'content into a shell.'
+              'system state or configuration, elevates privileges, writes to ' +
+              'raw devices, kills processes, rewrites published history, or ' +
+              'pipes remote content into a shell.'
           },
           dangerReason: {
             type: 'string',
-            description: 'Why the command is dangerous (when it is).'
+            description: 'A short reason the command is dangerous; give one whenever "dangerous" is true.'
           }
         },
         required: ['command', 'explanation', 'dangerous'],
@@ -144,11 +144,7 @@ export function buildSystem(opts: SystemPromptOptions): string {
 
   if (opts.structured) {
     rules.push(
-      'Assess whether the command is dangerous: anything that deletes or ' +
-        'overwrites data, changes system state or configuration, elevates ' +
-        'privileges, writes to raw devices, kills processes, rewrites ' +
-        'published history, or pipes remote content into a shell. Set the "dangerous" ' +
-        'field accordingly and give a short "dangerReason" when it is true.',
+      'Assess every command for danger and fill "dangerous" and "dangerReason" as their field descriptions define.',
       'The "explanation" field is one concise sentence in plain language.',
       'Each "command" field must contain the raw command text only - no ' +
         'markdown, no code fences, no surrounding quotes.'
diff --git a/test/prompts.test.ts b/test/prompts.test.ts
index 9c4ead9..20116ce 100644
--- a/test/prompts.test.ts
+++ b/test/prompts.test.ts
@@ -37,6 +37,15 @@ describe('buildSystem', () => {
     expect(system).toMatch(/danger/i)
   })
 
+  test('leaves the danger definition to the schema, so the two cannot disagree', () => {
+    const system = buildSystem(baseSystemOpts)
+    const properties = COMMANDS_SCHEMA.properties as Record<string, Record<string, unknown>>
+    const items = properties.commands?.items as { properties: Record<string, { description: string }> }
+    const definition = items.properties.dangerous?.description ?? ''
+    expect(definition).toContain('raw devices')
+    expect(system).not.toContain('raw devices')
+  })
+
   test('appends the custom prompt', () => {
     const system = buildSystem({
       ...baseSystemOpts,
